window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY=window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY||{};window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY["elevenlabs-game-audio.en"]=[{"body": "# ElevenLabs game audio\n\nDate: 2026-09-27 · [한국어](ElevenLabs_Game_Audio.md)\n\nThis work replaces the existing 283 sound cues, their 469 variations and four music contexts—title, sanctuary, rift and boss—with ElevenLabs audio. Effect IDs and gameplay routing stay intact; edited generated audio replaces the preceding DSP WAV files. Music now uses imported assets selected by game context.\n\nCompletion and runtime verification are recorded below. Generation, integration, signal inspection, human listening approval and integration into main are separate states.\n\n## Current integration and priorities\n\nThe full target is **287 cue types and 473 files**: 283 effects with 469 variations, plus four music tracks. The work branch currently contains 264 adopted effect cues with 433 variations and all four music tracks: **268/287 types (93.4%)**, or **437/473 files (92.4%)**. These are integration counts, not listening approval or integration into `main`.\n\nThe remaining 19 cues retain 36 legacy effect files. Three have one generated candidate each but still need a second distinct variation before adoption. There are 1,049 generated candidates in total; candidate counts are not added to completed integration counts.\n\nThe [production priority inventory](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json) records every target's status and the next production order. Shared UI, basic attacks, impacts, damage feedback and frequent pickups have priority. Whirlwind ticks, slash and metal impacts, hero hurt and gold pickup from an earlier macOS trace have been replaced. That trace is a development sample with unequal play time per class, not a population usage statistic.\n\nNext are `ui.click_primary`, `ui.tab`, `ui.open`, `ui.close`, `ui.error`, `ui.confirm`, `ui.click_heavy`, `ui.slider`, `ui.disabled` and `ui.notify`. Gambling beats, gem socketing, rune placement/rotation/removal/fusion/unlocking and reward box/claim sounds follow.\n\nThe provider returned `429 daily_generation_limit_reached`, so additional generation stopped. This daily quota is separate from remaining credits; its exact reset time is unverified. Paid requests are not automatically repeated. Filling the outstanding runtime variations requires at least 33 additional distinct generation results; unsuitable candidates may require further work.\n\n## Production and provenance\n\n| Property | Sound effects | Music |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Model returned by the official MCP | `eleven_text_to_sound_v2` | `eleven_music_v2` |\n| Generated source | MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps | MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps |\n| Edited runtime master | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo |\n| Unity import | Existing effect `.meta` files and GUIDs retained: ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory | Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, background loading, no preload |\n| Review state | Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending | Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending |\n\nThe generated source is already lossy MP3. WAV conversion supports editing and importing; it does not restore information or make generation lossless. Selected MP3s are retained outside the Unity build under `AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources`.\n\nThe [source manifest](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json) records provider, verified model, generation ID, full prompt, generation parameters, source/master SHA-256, processing and listening-review status for every asset. Credentials and temporary download URLs are excluded.\n\nPrompts distinguish weapons, materials, elements, creatures and actions. They cover all 54 skills and separate landing, explosion, trap, chain and summon events. Hero vocalizations are nonverbal effort, pain, death and breathing: an adult male warrior, a low husky adult female ranger and a clear mid-register adult female mage. No specific person's voice or existing game's recording was cloned or uploaded.\n\n## Editing for the game\n\nEffects with severe phase cancellation on mono summing are rejected. Unnecessary leading/trailing silence is trimmed, low-frequency DC is filtered, and short boundary fades are applied. Per-cue loudness targets follow the existing bank, with linear gain capped at -2 dBTP using four-times oversampling. No saturation or nonlinear compression is used to inflate loudness. Each runtime variation has a distinct generation.\n\nMusic joins its ending to its beginning with a 2.5-second crossfade and shifts the loop start to retain contiguous source samples at the final boundary. This addresses waveform discontinuities; it does not establish perceptual harmony, rhythm or musical-loop approval.\n\n| Context | Edited duration | Measured loudness | Measured true peak |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Title and character selection | 147.5 s | -20.01 LUFS | -3.00 dBTP |\n| Sanctuary and results | 177.5 s | -22.01 LUFS | -4.43 dBTP |\n| Rift exploration and looting | 177.5 s | -23.00 LUFS | -6.28 dBTP |\n| Boss combat | 147.5 s | -20.99 LUFS | -4.48 dBTP |\n\nMeasurements describe WAV masters before Unity compression. Runtime gain uses the existing master/music preferences; context transitions take 1.5 seconds. Deselected streams pause after fading out and resume when selected again. The application-pause callback suspends playback, and resume continues it. The playback owner stops its sources without destroying shared imported clips.\n\nEffects retain the existing 16-source pool, priorities, cooldowns, concurrency limits, attenuation, panning and final-mix limiter. Audio observes combat and committed transactions without mutating saves or consuming combat randomness. The [existing event routes](Sound_Effects_Bank.en.md) remain in use.\n\n## Offline reproduction and protection\n\n```sh\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check --allow-partial\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --audition Artifacts/Audio\n```\n\nThe explicit `--allow-partial` check validates adopted assets while reporting the 36 legacy files. Without that flag, `--check` requires all 473 assets and currently fails the completion gate. A partial validation pass is not full bank completion.\n\n[`elevenlabs_audio.py`](../../tools/elevenlabs_audio.py) `--rebuild` reproduces runtime masters from committed originals and their source manifest. It requires no API authentication, new generation or credits. All source hashes are preflighted before replacement; each master and manifest is replaced through a temporary file. Already matching assets are left alone.\n\nThe legacy synthesizer refuses to overwrite adopted ElevenLabs assets. Missing provenance fails closed instead of reverting to synthesized sounds. Checks, audits and audition output read the actual committed masters. New audio generation is a separate operation. Editing requires Python 3.9 or later, NumPy, SciPy and ffmpeg; the game does not.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidation used Unity 6000.6.0f1 in the isolated worktree, without using the user's running original Editor or save account. The macOS development build succeeded with zero build errors.\n\n| Check | Observed result | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Provenance and integration | 437 masters and original hashes validated; 36 legacy files retained | [Integration](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/integration-summary.json), [partial validation](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/partial-source-validation.json) |\n| Full replacement gate | Still fails: 36 ElevenLabs masters remain missing | [Completion gate](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/full-completion-gate.json) |\n| Effect signal | All 433 adopted effects pass; zero clipped samples; maximum absolute DC 0.000260; true peak approximately -2 dBTP | [Master audit](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json) |\n| Music signal | Four tracks pass; zero clipped samples; mono summing and loop boundary inspected | [Music audit](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json) |\n| Unity Edit Mode | 85 related cases pass, zero failures/skips: bank, music, real audio routes for 54 skills and buttons | [Per-case results](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-summary.json) |\n| Offline tools | Four tests pass for preflight preservation, path boundaries, signal editing and legacy tamper detection. Rebuild rerun retains all 437 hashes with zero generation calls | [Idempotence audit](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/offline-rebuild-audit.json) |\n| macOS music and preferences | Four streams advance, wrap and transition; volume/mute work and persist across separate native processes | [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt), [controls](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt), [restart](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt) |\n| macOS gameplay | Tutorial, three classes, pickups, equipment, town and settings produce 1,243 playback events across 83 cues: 75 adopted and eight legacy cues; zero logged errors | [Summary](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-summary.txt), [scope](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-scope.json), [trace](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-trace.tsv) |\n\nThe full 283-cue, 469-file effects bank was checked as a mixture of adopted and retained legacy audio. All existing effect `.meta` files and GUIDs remain intact. The shared UI contract and its nine Python tests also pass. Earlier DSP-bank runtime results are not added to the new assets' results.\n\nRuntime input uses synthetic EventSystem events. Some covered town controls were invoked through their callbacks, and a successful equip drag into a valid slot was not observed in this run. The music suspension check invokes the application-pause callback; it does not exercise actual OS suspension. The short music/skill fixture marks a disposable account past the prologue, while the longer effects fixture follows the actual tutorial flow.\n\n![Korean portrait audio preferences](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/01-audio-ko.png)\n\n![English landscape audio preferences](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/02-audio-en.png)\n\nThese results belong to the work branch. Integration into `main` and public wiki deployment have not occurred; publishing is restricted to merged `main`.\n\nHuman review of timbre, vocalization, timing, fatigue and musical repetition remains separate, as do physical mobile output and suspend/resume checks. Generation success and signal measurements alone do not establish highest quality or release approval.\n", "html": "<p>Date: 2026-09-27 · <a href=\"#/page/elevenlabs-game-audio\">한국어<\/a><\/p><p>This work replaces the existing 283 sound cues, their 469 variations and four music contexts—title, sanctuary, rift and boss—with ElevenLabs audio. Effect IDs and gameplay routing stay intact; edited generated audio replaces the preceding DSP WAV files. Music now uses imported assets selected by game context.<\/p><p>Completion and runtime verification are recorded below. Generation, integration, signal inspection, human listening approval and integration into main are separate states.<\/p><h2 id=\"current-integration-and-priorities\">Current integration and priorities<\/h2><p>The full target is <strong>287 cue types and 473 files<\/strong>: 283 effects with 469 variations, plus four music tracks. The work branch currently contains 264 adopted effect cues with 433 variations and all four music tracks: <strong>268/287 types (93.4%)<\/strong>, or <strong>437/473 files (92.4%)<\/strong>. These are integration counts, not listening approval or integration into <code>main<\/code>.<\/p><p>The remaining 19 cues retain 36 legacy effect files. Three have one generated candidate each but still need a second distinct variation before adoption. There are 1,049 generated candidates in total; candidate counts are not added to completed integration counts.<\/p><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json\">production priority inventory<\/a> records every target&#x27;s status and the next production order. Shared UI, basic attacks, impacts, damage feedback and frequent pickups have priority. Whirlwind ticks, slash and metal impacts, hero hurt and gold pickup from an earlier macOS trace have been replaced. That trace is a development sample with unequal play time per class, not a population usage statistic.<\/p><p>Next are <code>ui.click_primary<\/code>, <code>ui.tab<\/code>, <code>ui.open<\/code>, <code>ui.close<\/code>, <code>ui.error<\/code>, <code>ui.confirm<\/code>, <code>ui.click_heavy<\/code>, <code>ui.slider<\/code>, <code>ui.disabled<\/code> and <code>ui.notify<\/code>. Gambling beats, gem socketing, rune placement/rotation/removal/fusion/unlocking and reward box/claim sounds follow.<\/p><p>The provider returned <code>429 daily_generation_limit_reached<\/code>, so additional generation stopped. This daily quota is separate from remaining credits; its exact reset time is unverified. Paid requests are not automatically repeated. Filling the outstanding runtime variations requires at least 33 additional distinct generation results; unsuitable candidates may require further work.<\/p><h2 id=\"production-and-provenance\">Production and provenance<\/h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Property<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Sound effects<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Music<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Model returned by the official MCP<\/td><td><code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2<\/code><\/td><td><code>eleven_music_v2<\/code><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Generated source<\/td><td>MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps<\/td><td>MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Edited runtime master<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Unity import<\/td><td>Existing effect <code>.meta<\/code> files and GUIDs retained: ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory<\/td><td>Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, background loading, no preload<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Review state<\/td><td>Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending<\/td><td>Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The generated source is already lossy MP3. WAV conversion supports editing and importing; it does not restore information or make generation lossless. Selected MP3s are retained outside the Unity build under <code>AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources<\/code>.<\/p><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json\">source manifest<\/a> records provider, verified model, generation ID, full prompt, generation parameters, source/master SHA-256, processing and listening-review status for every asset. Credentials and temporary download URLs are excluded.<\/p><p>Prompts distinguish weapons, materials, elements, creatures and actions. They cover all 54 skills and separate landing, explosion, trap, chain and summon events. Hero vocalizations are nonverbal effort, pain, death and breathing: an adult male warrior, a low husky adult female ranger and a clear mid-register adult female mage. No specific person&#x27;s voice or existing game&#x27;s recording was cloned or uploaded.<\/p><h2 id=\"editing-for-the-game\">Editing for the game<\/h2><p>Effects with severe phase cancellation on mono summing are rejected. Unnecessary leading/trailing silence is trimmed, low-frequency DC is filtered, and short boundary fades are applied. Per-cue loudness targets follow the existing bank, with linear gain capped at -2 dBTP using four-times oversampling. No saturation or nonlinear compression is used to inflate loudness. Each runtime variation has a distinct generation.<\/p><p>Music joins its ending to its beginning with a 2.5-second crossfade and shifts the loop start to retain contiguous source samples at the final boundary. This addresses waveform discontinuities; it does not establish perceptual harmony, rhythm or musical-loop approval.<\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Context<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Edited duration<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Measured loudness<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Measured true peak<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Title and character selection<\/td><td>147.5 s<\/td><td>-20.01 LUFS<\/td><td>-3.00 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Sanctuary and results<\/td><td>177.5 s<\/td><td>-22.01 LUFS<\/td><td>-4.43 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Rift exploration and looting<\/td><td>177.5 s<\/td><td>-23.00 LUFS<\/td><td>-6.28 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Boss combat<\/td><td>147.5 s<\/td><td>-20.99 LUFS<\/td><td>-4.48 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>Measurements describe WAV masters before Unity compression. Runtime gain uses the existing master/music preferences; context transitions take 1.5 seconds. Deselected streams pause after fading out and resume when selected again. The application-pause callback suspends playback, and resume continues it. The playback owner stops its sources without destroying shared imported clips.<\/p><p>Effects retain the existing 16-source pool, priorities, cooldowns, concurrency limits, attenuation, panning and final-mix limiter. Audio observes combat and committed transactions without mutating saves or consuming combat randomness. The <a href=\"#/page/sound-effects-bank.en\">existing event routes<\/a> remain in use.<\/p><h2 id=\"offline-reproduction-and-protection\">Offline reproduction and protection<\/h2><pre><code>python3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check --allow-partial\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --audition Artifacts/Audio<\/code><\/pre><p>The explicit <code>--allow-partial<\/code> check validates adopted assets while reporting the 36 legacy files. Without that flag, <code>--check<\/code> requires all 473 assets and currently fails the completion gate. A partial validation pass is not full bank completion.<\/p><p><a href=\"sources/tools/elevenlabs_audio.py\">`elevenlabs_audio.py`<\/a> <code>--rebuild<\/code> reproduces runtime masters from committed originals and their source manifest. It requires no API authentication, new generation or credits. All source hashes are preflighted before replacement; each master and manifest is replaced through a temporary file. Already matching assets are left alone.<\/p><p>The legacy synthesizer refuses to overwrite adopted ElevenLabs assets. Missing provenance fails closed instead of reverting to synthesized sounds. Checks, audits and audition output read the actual committed masters. New audio generation is a separate operation. Editing requires Python 3.9 or later, NumPy, SciPy and ffmpeg; the game does not.<\/p><h2 id=\"validation\">Validation<\/h2><p>Validation used Unity 6000.6.0f1 in the isolated worktree, without using the user&#x27;s running original Editor or save account. The macOS development build succeeded with zero build errors.<\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Check<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Observed result<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Evidence<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Provenance and integration<\/td><td>437 masters and original hashes validated; 36 legacy files retained<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/integration-summary.json\">Integration<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/partial-source-validation.json\">partial validation<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Full replacement gate<\/td><td>Still fails: 36 ElevenLabs masters remain missing<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/full-completion-gate.json\">Completion gate<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Effect signal<\/td><td>All 433 adopted effects pass; zero clipped samples; maximum absolute DC 0.000260; true peak approximately -2 dBTP<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json\">Master audit<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Music signal<\/td><td>Four tracks pass; zero clipped samples; mono summing and loop boundary inspected<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json\">Music audit<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Unity Edit Mode<\/td><td>85 related cases pass, zero failures/skips: bank, music, real audio routes for 54 skills and buttons<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-summary.json\">Per-case results<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Offline tools<\/td><td>Four tests pass for preflight preservation, path boundaries, signal editing and legacy tamper detection. Rebuild rerun retains all 437 hashes with zero generation calls<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/offline-rebuild-audit.json\">Idempotence audit<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>macOS music and preferences<\/td><td>Four streams advance, wrap and transition; volume/mute work and persist across separate native processes<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt\">Music<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt\">controls<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt\">restart<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>macOS gameplay<\/td><td>Tutorial, three classes, pickups, equipment, town and settings produce 1,243 playback events across 83 cues: 75 adopted and eight legacy cues; zero logged errors<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-summary.txt\">Summary<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-scope.json\">scope<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-trace.tsv\">trace<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The full 283-cue, 469-file effects bank was checked as a mixture of adopted and retained legacy audio. All existing effect <code>.meta<\/code> files and GUIDs remain intact. The shared UI contract and its nine Python tests also pass. Earlier DSP-bank runtime results are not added to the new assets&#x27; results.<\/p><p>Runtime input uses synthetic EventSystem events. Some covered town controls were invoked through their callbacks, and a successful equip drag into a valid slot was not observed in this run. The music suspension check invokes the application-pause callback; it does not exercise actual OS suspension. The short music/skill fixture marks a disposable account past the prologue, while the longer effects fixture follows the actual tutorial flow.<\/p><p><img class=\"evidence-image\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/01-audio-ko.png\" alt=\"Korean portrait audio preferences\"><\/p><p><img class=\"evidence-image\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/02-audio-en.png\" alt=\"English landscape audio preferences\"><\/p><p>These results belong to the work branch. Integration into <code>main<\/code> and public wiki deployment have not occurred; publishing is restricted to merged <code>main<\/code>.<\/p><p>Human review of timbre, vocalization, timing, fatigue and musical repetition remains separate, as do physical mobile output and suspend/resume checks. Generation success and signal measurements alone do not establish highest quality or release approval.<\/p>", "headings": [{"id": "current-integration-and-priorities", "title": "Current integration and priorities"}, {"id": "production-and-provenance", "title": "Production and provenance"}, {"id": "editing-for-the-game", "title": "Editing for the game"}, {"id": "offline-reproduction-and-protection", "title": "Offline reproduction and protection"}, {"id": "validation", "title": "Validation"}]}, {"body": "# ElevenLabs game audio\n\nDate: 2026-09-27 · [한국어](ElevenLabs_Game_Audio.md)\n\nThis work replaces the existing 283 sound cues, their 469 variations and four music contexts—title, sanctuary, rift and boss—with ElevenLabs audio. Effect IDs and gameplay routing stay intact; edited generated audio replaces the preceding DSP WAV files. Music now uses imported assets selected by game context.\n\nCompletion and runtime verification are recorded below. Generation, integration, signal inspection, human listening approval and integration into main are separate states.\n\n## Current integration and priorities\n\nThe full target is **287 cue types and 473 files**: 283 effects with 469 variations, plus four music tracks. The work branch currently contains 274 adopted effect cues with 454 variations and all four music tracks: **278/287 types (96.9%)**, or **458/473 files (96.8%)**. These are integration counts, not listening approval or integration into `main`.\n\nThe remaining nine cues retain 15 legacy effect files. Three have one generated candidate each but still need a second distinct variation before adoption. There are 1,087 generated candidates in total; candidate counts are not added to completed integration counts.\n\nThe [production priority inventory](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json) records every target's status and the next production order. Shared UI, basic attacks, impacts, damage feedback and frequent pickups have priority. Whirlwind ticks, slash and metal impacts, hero hurt and gold pickup from an earlier macOS trace have been replaced. That trace is a development sample with unequal play time per class, not a population usage statistic.\n\nThis continuation added 21 files across ten cues: `ui.click_primary`, `ui.tab`, `ui.open`, `ui.close`, `ui.error`, `ui.confirm`, `ui.click_heavy`, `ui.slider`, `ui.disabled` and `ui.notify`. It produced 38 candidates and preserved the previously adopted 437 assets unchanged. Reward claims and boxes, gambling beats, gem socketing and rune placement/rotation/removal/fusion/unlocking remain next. [Continuation record](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-continuation-summary.json)\n\nThe provider returned `429 daily_generation_limit_reached`, so additional generation stopped. This daily quota is separate from remaining credits; its exact reset time is unverified. Paid requests are not automatically repeated. Filling the outstanding runtime variations requires at least 12 additional distinct generation results; unsuitable candidates may require further work.\n\n## Production and provenance\n\n| Property | Sound effects | Music |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Model returned by the official MCP | `eleven_text_to_sound_v2` | `eleven_music_v2` |\n| Generated source | MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps | MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps |\n| Edited runtime master | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo |\n| Unity import | Existing effect `.meta` files and GUIDs retained: ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory | Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, background loading, no preload |\n| Review state | Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending | Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending |\n\nThe generated source is already lossy MP3. WAV conversion supports editing and importing; it does not restore information or make generation lossless. Selected MP3s are retained outside the Unity build under `AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources`.\n\nThe [source manifest](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json) records provider, verified model, generation ID, full prompt, generation parameters, source/master SHA-256, processing and listening-review status for every asset. Credentials and temporary download URLs are excluded.\n\nPrompts distinguish weapons, materials, elements, creatures and actions. They cover all 54 skills and separate landing, explosion, trap, chain and summon events. Hero vocalizations are nonverbal effort, pain, death and breathing: an adult male warrior, a low husky adult female ranger and a clear mid-register adult female mage. No specific person's voice or existing game's recording was cloned or uploaded.\n\n## Editing for the game\n\nEffects with severe phase cancellation on mono summing are rejected. Unnecessary leading/trailing silence is trimmed, low-frequency DC is filtered, and short boundary fades are applied. Per-cue loudness targets follow the existing bank, with linear gain capped at -2 dBTP using four-times oversampling. No saturation or nonlinear compression is used to inflate loudness. Each runtime variation has a distinct generation.\n\nRepeated ratchet clicks in slider sources are cut to one 30 ms tick, shorter than the existing 50 ms cooldown. Tab sources are trimmed past quiet leading noise so the main attack arrives promptly: the selected variants reach 5% cumulative energy after roughly 5–19 ms. Original sources and edit windows remain in the manifest, and reproduction needs no new generation. [UI timing evidence](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-transient-edit.json)\n\nMusic joins its ending to its beginning with a 2.5-second crossfade and shifts the loop start to retain contiguous source samples at the final boundary. This addresses waveform discontinuities; it does not establish perceptual harmony, rhythm or musical-loop approval.\n\n| Context | Edited duration | Measured loudness | Measured true peak |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Title and character selection | 147.5 s | -20.01 LUFS | -3.00 dBTP |\n| Sanctuary and results | 177.5 s | -22.01 LUFS | -4.43 dBTP |\n| Rift exploration and looting | 177.5 s | -23.00 LUFS | -6.28 dBTP |\n| Boss combat | 147.5 s | -20.99 LUFS | -4.48 dBTP |\n\nMeasurements describe WAV masters before Unity compression. Runtime gain uses the existing master/music preferences; context transitions take 1.5 seconds. Deselected streams pause after fading out and resume when selected again. The application-pause callback suspends playback, and resume continues it. The playback owner stops its sources without destroying shared imported clips.\n\nEffects retain the existing 16-source pool, priorities, cooldowns, concurrency limits, attenuation, panning and final-mix limiter. Audio observes combat and committed transactions without mutating saves or consuming combat randomness. The [existing event routes](Sound_Effects_Bank.en.md) remain in use.\n\n## Offline reproduction and protection\n\n```sh\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check --allow-partial\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --audition Artifacts/Audio\n```\n\nThe explicit `--allow-partial` check validates adopted assets while reporting the 15 legacy files. Without that flag, `--check` requires all 473 assets and currently fails the completion gate. A partial validation pass is not full bank completion.\n\n[`elevenlabs_audio.py`](../../tools/elevenlabs_audio.py) `--rebuild` reproduces runtime masters from committed originals and their source manifest. It requires no API authentication, new generation or credits. All source hashes are preflighted before replacement; each master and manifest is replaced through a temporary file. Already matching assets are left alone.\n\nThe legacy synthesizer refuses to overwrite adopted ElevenLabs assets. Missing provenance fails closed instead of reverting to synthesized sounds. Checks, audits and audition output read the actual committed masters. New audio generation is a separate operation. Editing requires Python 3.9 or later, NumPy, SciPy and ffmpeg; the game does not.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidation used Unity 6000.6.0f1 in the isolated worktree, without using the user's running original Editor or save account. The macOS development build succeeded with zero build errors.\n\n| Check | Observed result | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Provenance and integration | 458 masters and original hashes validated; 15 legacy files retained | [Integration](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/integration-summary.json), [partial validation](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/partial-source-validation.json) |\n| Full replacement gate | Still fails: 15 ElevenLabs masters remain missing | [Completion gate](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/full-completion-gate.json) |\n| Effect signal | All 454 adopted effects pass; zero clipped samples; maximum absolute DC 0.000260; true peak approximately -2 dBTP | [Master audit](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json) |\n| Music signal | Four tracks pass; zero clipped samples; mono summing and loop boundary inspected | [Music audit](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json) |\n| Unity Edit Mode | 85 cases passed for the initial integration. After UI sound editing, 30 bank/button cases passed again with zero failures/skips | [Initial cases](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-summary.json), [UI follow-up cases](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-ui-resume-summary.json) |\n| Offline tools | Six tests pass for preflight preservation, path boundaries, signal editing, legacy tamper detection and UI timing. Rebuild rerun retains all 458 hashes with zero generation calls | [Idempotence audit](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/offline-rebuild-audit.json) |\n| macOS music and preferences | Four streams advance, wrap and transition; volume/mute work and persist across separate native processes | [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt), [controls](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt), [restart](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt) |\n| macOS gameplay | Post-UI-edit run: tutorial, three classes, inventory, gambling and settings produce 1,230 events across 86 cues: 85 adopted and one legacy cue; zero logged errors. Optional forge interaction skipped because its pointer target was covered | [Summary](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-summary.txt), [scope](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-scope.json), [trace](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-trace.tsv) |\n\nThe full 283-cue, 469-file effects bank was checked as a mixture of adopted and retained legacy audio. All existing effect `.meta` files and GUIDs remain intact. The shared UI contract and its nine Python tests also pass. Earlier DSP-bank runtime results are not added to the new assets' results.\n\nRuntime input uses synthetic EventSystem events. Some covered town controls were invoked through their callbacks. The optional forge phase was skipped because its pointer target was covered; a successful equip drag into a valid slot was not observed in this run. The music suspension check invokes the application-pause callback; it does not exercise actual OS suspension. The short music/skill fixture marks a disposable account past the prologue, while the longer effects fixture follows the actual tutorial flow.\n\n![Korean portrait audio preferences](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/01-audio-ko.png)\n\n![English landscape audio preferences](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/02-audio-en.png)\n\nThese results belong to the work branch. Integration into `main` and public wiki deployment have not occurred; publishing is restricted to merged `main`.\n\nHuman review of timbre, vocalization, timing, fatigue and musical repetition remains separate, as do physical mobile output and suspend/resume checks. Generation success and signal measurements alone do not establish highest quality or release approval.\n", "html": "<p>Date: 2026-09-27 · <a href=\"#/page/elevenlabs-game-audio\">한국어<\/a><\/p><p>This work replaces the existing 283 sound cues, their 469 variations and four music contexts—title, sanctuary, rift and boss—with ElevenLabs audio. Effect IDs and gameplay routing stay intact; edited generated audio replaces the preceding DSP WAV files. Music now uses imported assets selected by game context.<\/p><p>Completion and runtime verification are recorded below. Generation, integration, signal inspection, human listening approval and integration into main are separate states.<\/p><h2 id=\"current-integration-and-priorities\">Current integration and priorities<\/h2><p>The full target is <strong>287 cue types and 473 files<\/strong>: 283 effects with 469 variations, plus four music tracks. The work branch currently contains 274 adopted effect cues with 454 variations and all four music tracks: <strong>278/287 types (96.9%)<\/strong>, or <strong>458/473 files (96.8%)<\/strong>. These are integration counts, not listening approval or integration into <code>main<\/code>.<\/p><p>The remaining nine cues retain 15 legacy effect files. Three have one generated candidate each but still need a second distinct variation before adoption. There are 1,087 generated candidates in total; candidate counts are not added to completed integration counts.<\/p><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json\">production priority inventory<\/a> records every target&#x27;s status and the next production order. Shared UI, basic attacks, impacts, damage feedback and frequent pickups have priority. Whirlwind ticks, slash and metal impacts, hero hurt and gold pickup from an earlier macOS trace have been replaced. That trace is a development sample with unequal play time per class, not a population usage statistic.<\/p><p>This continuation added 21 files across ten cues: <code>ui.click_primary<\/code>, <code>ui.tab<\/code>, <code>ui.open<\/code>, <code>ui.close<\/code>, <code>ui.error<\/code>, <code>ui.confirm<\/code>, <code>ui.click_heavy<\/code>, <code>ui.slider<\/code>, <code>ui.disabled<\/code> and <code>ui.notify<\/code>. It produced 38 candidates and preserved the previously adopted 437 assets unchanged. Reward claims and boxes, gambling beats, gem socketing and rune placement/rotation/removal/fusion/unlocking remain next. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-continuation-summary.json\">Continuation record<\/a><\/p><p>The provider returned <code>429 daily_generation_limit_reached<\/code>, so additional generation stopped. This daily quota is separate from remaining credits; its exact reset time is unverified. Paid requests are not automatically repeated. Filling the outstanding runtime variations requires at least 12 additional distinct generation results; unsuitable candidates may require further work.<\/p><h2 id=\"production-and-provenance\">Production and provenance<\/h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Property<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Sound effects<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Music<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Model returned by the official MCP<\/td><td><code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2<\/code><\/td><td><code>eleven_music_v2<\/code><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Generated source<\/td><td>MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps<\/td><td>MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Edited runtime master<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Unity import<\/td><td>Existing effect <code>.meta<\/code> files and GUIDs retained: ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory<\/td><td>Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, background loading, no preload<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Review state<\/td><td>Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending<\/td><td>Signal checks and technical candidate selection; human listening pending<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The generated source is already lossy MP3. WAV conversion supports editing and importing; it does not restore information or make generation lossless. Selected MP3s are retained outside the Unity build under <code>AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources<\/code>.<\/p><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json\">source manifest<\/a> records provider, verified model, generation ID, full prompt, generation parameters, source/master SHA-256, processing and listening-review status for every asset. Credentials and temporary download URLs are excluded.<\/p><p>Prompts distinguish weapons, materials, elements, creatures and actions. They cover all 54 skills and separate landing, explosion, trap, chain and summon events. Hero vocalizations are nonverbal effort, pain, death and breathing: an adult male warrior, a low husky adult female ranger and a clear mid-register adult female mage. No specific person&#x27;s voice or existing game&#x27;s recording was cloned or uploaded.<\/p><h2 id=\"editing-for-the-game\">Editing for the game<\/h2><p>Effects with severe phase cancellation on mono summing are rejected. Unnecessary leading/trailing silence is trimmed, low-frequency DC is filtered, and short boundary fades are applied. Per-cue loudness targets follow the existing bank, with linear gain capped at -2 dBTP using four-times oversampling. No saturation or nonlinear compression is used to inflate loudness. Each runtime variation has a distinct generation.<\/p><p>Repeated ratchet clicks in slider sources are cut to one 30 ms tick, shorter than the existing 50 ms cooldown. Tab sources are trimmed past quiet leading noise so the main attack arrives promptly: the selected variants reach 5% cumulative energy after roughly 5–19 ms. Original sources and edit windows remain in the manifest, and reproduction needs no new generation. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-transient-edit.json\">UI timing evidence<\/a><\/p><p>Music joins its ending to its beginning with a 2.5-second crossfade and shifts the loop start to retain contiguous source samples at the final boundary. This addresses waveform discontinuities; it does not establish perceptual harmony, rhythm or musical-loop approval.<\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Context<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Edited duration<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Measured loudness<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Measured true peak<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Title and character selection<\/td><td>147.5 s<\/td><td>-20.01 LUFS<\/td><td>-3.00 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Sanctuary and results<\/td><td>177.5 s<\/td><td>-22.01 LUFS<\/td><td>-4.43 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Rift exploration and looting<\/td><td>177.5 s<\/td><td>-23.00 LUFS<\/td><td>-6.28 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Boss combat<\/td><td>147.5 s<\/td><td>-20.99 LUFS<\/td><td>-4.48 dBTP<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>Measurements describe WAV masters before Unity compression. Runtime gain uses the existing master/music preferences; context transitions take 1.5 seconds. Deselected streams pause after fading out and resume when selected again. The application-pause callback suspends playback, and resume continues it. The playback owner stops its sources without destroying shared imported clips.<\/p><p>Effects retain the existing 16-source pool, priorities, cooldowns, concurrency limits, attenuation, panning and final-mix limiter. Audio observes combat and committed transactions without mutating saves or consuming combat randomness. The <a href=\"#/page/sound-effects-bank.en\">existing event routes<\/a> remain in use.<\/p><h2 id=\"offline-reproduction-and-protection\">Offline reproduction and protection<\/h2><pre><code>python3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check --allow-partial\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --audition Artifacts/Audio<\/code><\/pre><p>The explicit <code>--allow-partial<\/code> check validates adopted assets while reporting the 15 legacy files. Without that flag, <code>--check<\/code> requires all 473 assets and currently fails the completion gate. A partial validation pass is not full bank completion.<\/p><p><a href=\"sources/tools/elevenlabs_audio.py\">`elevenlabs_audio.py`<\/a> <code>--rebuild<\/code> reproduces runtime masters from committed originals and their source manifest. It requires no API authentication, new generation or credits. All source hashes are preflighted before replacement; each master and manifest is replaced through a temporary file. Already matching assets are left alone.<\/p><p>The legacy synthesizer refuses to overwrite adopted ElevenLabs assets. Missing provenance fails closed instead of reverting to synthesized sounds. Checks, audits and audition output read the actual committed masters. New audio generation is a separate operation. Editing requires Python 3.9 or later, NumPy, SciPy and ffmpeg; the game does not.<\/p><h2 id=\"validation\">Validation<\/h2><p>Validation used Unity 6000.6.0f1 in the isolated worktree, without using the user&#x27;s running original Editor or save account. The macOS development build succeeded with zero build errors.<\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Check<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Observed result<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Evidence<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Provenance and integration<\/td><td>458 masters and original hashes validated; 15 legacy files retained<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/integration-summary.json\">Integration<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/partial-source-validation.json\">partial validation<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Full replacement gate<\/td><td>Still fails: 15 ElevenLabs masters remain missing<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/full-completion-gate.json\">Completion gate<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Effect signal<\/td><td>All 454 adopted effects pass; zero clipped samples; maximum absolute DC 0.000260; true peak approximately -2 dBTP<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json\">Master audit<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Music signal<\/td><td>Four tracks pass; zero clipped samples; mono summing and loop boundary inspected<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json\">Music audit<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Unity Edit Mode<\/td><td>85 cases passed for the initial integration. After UI sound editing, 30 bank/button cases passed again with zero failures/skips<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-summary.json\">Initial cases<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-ui-resume-summary.json\">UI follow-up cases<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Offline tools<\/td><td>Six tests pass for preflight preservation, path boundaries, signal editing, legacy tamper detection and UI timing. Rebuild rerun retains all 458 hashes with zero generation calls<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/offline-rebuild-audit.json\">Idempotence audit<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>macOS music and preferences<\/td><td>Four streams advance, wrap and transition; volume/mute work and persist across separate native processes<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt\">Music<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt\">controls<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt\">restart<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>macOS gameplay<\/td><td>Post-UI-edit run: tutorial, three classes, inventory, gambling and settings produce 1,230 events across 86 cues: 85 adopted and one legacy cue; zero logged errors. Optional forge interaction skipped because its pointer target was covered<\/td><td><a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-summary.txt\">Summary<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-scope.json\">scope<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-sfx-trace.tsv\">trace<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The full 283-cue, 469-file effects bank was checked as a mixture of adopted and retained legacy audio. All existing effect <code>.meta<\/code> files and GUIDs remain intact. The shared UI contract and its nine Python tests also pass. Earlier DSP-bank runtime results are not added to the new assets&#x27; results.<\/p><p>Runtime input uses synthetic EventSystem events. Some covered town controls were invoked through their callbacks. The optional forge phase was skipped because its pointer target was covered; a successful equip drag into a valid slot was not observed in this run. The music suspension check invokes the application-pause callback; it does not exercise actual OS suspension. The short music/skill fixture marks a disposable account past the prologue, while the longer effects fixture follows the actual tutorial flow.<\/p><p><img class=\"evidence-image\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/01-audio-ko.png\" alt=\"Korean portrait audio preferences\"><\/p><p><img class=\"evidence-image\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/02-audio-en.png\" alt=\"English landscape audio preferences\"><\/p><p>These results belong to the work branch. Integration into <code>main<\/code> and public wiki deployment have not occurred; publishing is restricted to merged <code>main<\/code>.<\/p><p>Human review of timbre, vocalization, timing, fatigue and musical repetition remains separate, as do physical mobile output and suspend/resume checks. Generation success and signal measurements alone do not establish highest quality or release approval.<\/p>", "headings": [{"id": "current-integration-and-priorities", "title": "Current integration and priorities"}, {"id": "production-and-provenance", "title": "Production and provenance"}, {"id": "editing-for-the-game", "title": "Editing for the game"}, {"id": "offline-reproduction-and-protection", "title": "Offline reproduction and protection"}, {"id": "validation", "title": "Validation"}]}, {"body": "# ElevenLabs game audio\n\nWritten: 2026-09-27 · [한국어](ElevenLabs_Game_Audio.md)\n\nThe user accepted the currently adopted audio as the final version. The retained set contains **454 sound effects and four music tracks: 458 files**. It covers all 283 SFX identifiers and four music contexts. Nine SFX actions share suitable existing final clips. No additional generation is planned.\n\nFinal acceptance is based on the user's instruction. It does not claim a new human listening test or physical mobile validation. These changes are on the work branch; merging to `main` and publishing the wiki are separate steps.\n\n## Final catalog and shared clips\n\n274 SFX identifiers have dedicated source generations. The following nine actions reference the same imported `AudioClip` assets as their source cues. They do not copy files or count the same generation as another variation. Action identifiers, cooldowns, priorities and concurrency limits remain intact.\n\n| Action | Final source cue | Reason |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `reward.claim` | `ui.confirm` | Successful reward confirmation |\n| `shop.gamble_beat` | `ui.click_heavy` | Short, weighty reveal beat |\n| `gem.socket` | `item.equip.orb` | A crystal seating in a metal mount |\n| `reward.box_open` | `reward.chest` | A treasure chest with a latch and wooden hinge |\n| `rune.fuse` | `gem.fuse` | Crystal tones converging into one |\n| `rune.place` | `forge.core_invest` | A stone core inserted into a slot |\n| `rune.remove` | `gem.remove` | A release click from a mounted material |\n| `rune.rotate` | `loot.stone` | A short mineral contact |\n| `rune.unlock` | `aspect.upgrade` | A rising arcane-seal resonance |\n\nThe [final catalog](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/sfx-catalog.json) owns mastering targets and shared-cue relationships. It produces the [runtime bank](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Resources/Audio/Sfx/bank.json). The [production list](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json) distinguishes dedicated and shared audio; the previous generation-limit wait is closed.\n\n## Removal and storage\n\n- Removed all 15 remaining procedural WAVs and their `.meta` files after checking for external Unity GUID references. The bytes, GUIDs and import settings of all 458 final assets are preserved.\n- Removed downloaded copies of all 1,087 generation candidates, old preview conversions, duplicated preview masters, previous test builds and temporary test saves. Exactly one retained original per selected generation remains under `AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources`.\n- Removed retired synthesis recipes and synthesis-only code. The historical `generate_sfx.py` command now validates final files, writes bank metadata and produces previews. Running it without an operation fails instead of synthesizing audio.\n- The audition page uses a symbolic link to the actual game masters. Rebuilding it does not duplicate WAV or MP3 files.\n- Git history is unchanged. Removed tracked files can be recovered from pre-cleanup commit `949b31af520249e3c7708c7ef96256099f293cf6`. Other worktrees and the general Unity cache are outside this cleanup.\n\nRetired runtime WAVs occupied 1,504,326 bytes. Final runtime WAVs total 176,891,768 bytes. Task production and validation artifacts decreased from approximately 3.00 GB to 13.7 MB, **saving about 2.98 GB**. The new validation build and temporary accounts were also removed. [Cleanup evidence](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json) records the measurements. Source-storage savings are not measurements of mobile build size or runtime memory savings.\n\n## Preserved provenance and audio quality\n\n| Item | SFX | Music |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MCP-verified model | `eleven_text_to_sound_v2` | `eleven_music_v2` |\n| Generated original | MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps | MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps |\n| Final master | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo |\n| Unity import | Existing ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory | Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, no preload |\n\nThe [source manifest](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json) records model, generation ID, prompt, parameters and source/master hashes. Originals remain outside Unity builds for reproduction and provenance. Converting an MP3 to WAV does not recover discarded information. Cleanup does not re-encode or reduce the quality of any retained master.\n\nSFX processing uses silence trimming, DC removal, short fades, linear gain and a -2 dBTP ceiling. Slider effects contain one 30 ms tick; the three tab variants reach 5% cumulative energy about 5–19 ms after onset. [UI edit evidence](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-transient-edit.json)\n\nMusic lengths are 147.5 seconds for title and boss, and 177.5 seconds for sanctuary and rift. The loop splice spans 2.5 seconds; context changes use a 1.5-second fade. Unselected music pauses. The existing 16 SFX voices, priorities, concurrency controls and final-mix limiter remain. Audio does not mutate saves or combat random streams.\n\n## Maintenance and validation\n\n```sh\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/audio_audition.py\n```\n\nThe full provenance check requires all 458 assets; a partial-completion option is no longer necessary. Retired or unreferenced runtime WAVs and modified originals or masters fail validation. `--rebuild` uses retained sources and skips shared actions, so it creates no duplicate audio. These tools make no API calls and spend no credits.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent cleanup validation is recorded in the [cleanup report](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json) and [Unity result](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-final-summary.json). Checks compare all 458 master hashes and metadata with the baseline, retain every playback identifier, and verify that shared actions play the same imported assets.\n\n31 Unity Edit Mode tests, seven offline tool tests and nine shared UI contract tests passed. The [full provenance check](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-source-validation.json) passed for all 458 files with none missing. The macOS development build succeeded with zero errors. Native focused checks passed for all nine shared effects using existing imported assets and listener output, four music transitions/loops, short developer-training runs for three classes, volume/mute and preferences restored after process restart. [Shared effects](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-shared-effects.txt) · [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-music.txt) · [Controls/classes](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-audio.txt) · [Restart](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-restart.txt)\n\nThe full gameplay smoke recorded 1,074 events across 76 cues with no missing clips or logged errors. However, after an optional inventory interaction failed, the ranger timed out approaching the rift keeper: **the full smoke failed**. Forge interaction was also skipped because its pointer target was blocked. Focused audio success is not substituted for full gameplay success. [Full summary](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-summary.txt) · [Trace](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-trace.tsv)\n\nEarlier signal measurements remain applicable to byte-identical masters: all 454 SFX passed with zero clipped samples, maximum absolute DC 0.000260 and approximately -2 dBTP peak. [SFX](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json) · [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json)\n\nEarlier music/settings runtime tests covered four streaming tracks, loop progress, transitions, volume, mute and settings restoration after process restart. [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt) · [Settings](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt) · [Restart](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt)\n\nThe macOS gameplay smoke uses synthetic EventSystem input and disposable accounts. Covered town controls may use direct callbacks; optional forge interaction is skipped if pointer access is blocked. This is not physical mobile input or performance evidence. The public wiki is published only from merged `main`.\n", "html": "<p>Written: 2026-09-27 · <a href=\"#/page/elevenlabs-game-audio\">한국어<\/a><\/p><p>The user accepted the currently adopted audio as the final version. The retained set contains <strong>454 sound effects and four music tracks: 458 files<\/strong>. It covers all 283 SFX identifiers and four music contexts. Nine SFX actions share suitable existing final clips. No additional generation is planned.<\/p><p>Final acceptance is based on the user&#x27;s instruction. It does not claim a new human listening test or physical mobile validation. These changes are on the work branch; merging to <code>main<\/code> and publishing the wiki are separate steps.<\/p><h2 id=\"final-catalog-and-shared-clips\">Final catalog and shared clips<\/h2><p>274 SFX identifiers have dedicated source generations. The following nine actions reference the same imported <code>AudioClip<\/code> assets as their source cues. They do not copy files or count the same generation as another variation. Action identifiers, cooldowns, priorities and concurrency limits remain intact.<\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Action<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Final source cue<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Reason<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><code>reward.claim<\/code><\/td><td><code>ui.confirm<\/code><\/td><td>Successful reward confirmation<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>shop.gamble_beat<\/code><\/td><td><code>ui.click_heavy<\/code><\/td><td>Short, weighty reveal beat<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>gem.socket<\/code><\/td><td><code>item.equip.orb<\/code><\/td><td>A crystal seating in a metal mount<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>reward.box_open<\/code><\/td><td><code>reward.chest<\/code><\/td><td>A treasure chest with a latch and wooden hinge<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.fuse<\/code><\/td><td><code>gem.fuse<\/code><\/td><td>Crystal tones converging into one<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.place<\/code><\/td><td><code>forge.core_invest<\/code><\/td><td>A stone core inserted into a slot<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.remove<\/code><\/td><td><code>gem.remove<\/code><\/td><td>A release click from a mounted material<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.rotate<\/code><\/td><td><code>loot.stone<\/code><\/td><td>A short mineral contact<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.unlock<\/code><\/td><td><code>aspect.upgrade<\/code><\/td><td>A rising arcane-seal resonance<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/sfx-catalog.json\">final catalog<\/a> owns mastering targets and shared-cue relationships. It produces the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Resources/Audio/Sfx/bank.json\">runtime bank<\/a>. The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json\">production list<\/a> distinguishes dedicated and shared audio; the previous generation-limit wait is closed.<\/p><h2 id=\"removal-and-storage\">Removal and storage<\/h2><ul><li>Removed all 15 remaining procedural WAVs and their <code>.meta<\/code> files after checking for external Unity GUID references. The bytes, GUIDs and import settings of all 458 final assets are preserved.<\/li><li>Removed downloaded copies of all 1,087 generation candidates, old preview conversions, duplicated preview masters, previous test builds and temporary test saves. Exactly one retained original per selected generation remains under <code>AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources<\/code>.<\/li><li>Removed retired synthesis recipes and synthesis-only code. The historical <code>generate_sfx.py<\/code> command now validates final files, writes bank metadata and produces previews. Running it without an operation fails instead of synthesizing audio.<\/li><li>The audition page uses a symbolic link to the actual game masters. Rebuilding it does not duplicate WAV or MP3 files.<\/li><li>Git history is unchanged. Removed tracked files can be recovered from pre-cleanup commit <code>949b31af520249e3c7708c7ef96256099f293cf6<\/code>. Other worktrees and the general Unity cache are outside this cleanup.<\/li><\/ul><p>Retired runtime WAVs occupied 1,504,326 bytes. Final runtime WAVs total 176,891,768 bytes. Task production and validation artifacts decreased from approximately 3.00 GB to 13.7 MB, <strong>saving about 2.98 GB<\/strong>. The new validation build and temporary accounts were also removed. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json\">Cleanup evidence<\/a> records the measurements. Source-storage savings are not measurements of mobile build size or runtime memory savings.<\/p><h2 id=\"preserved-provenance-and-audio-quality\">Preserved provenance and audio quality<\/h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Item<\/th><th scope=\"col\">SFX<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Music<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>MCP-verified model<\/td><td><code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2<\/code><\/td><td><code>eleven_music_v2<\/code><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Generated original<\/td><td>MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps<\/td><td>MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Final master<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Unity import<\/td><td>Existing ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory<\/td><td>Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, no preload<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json\">source manifest<\/a> records model, generation ID, prompt, parameters and source/master hashes. Originals remain outside Unity builds for reproduction and provenance. Converting an MP3 to WAV does not recover discarded information. Cleanup does not re-encode or reduce the quality of any retained master.<\/p><p>SFX processing uses silence trimming, DC removal, short fades, linear gain and a -2 dBTP ceiling. Slider effects contain one 30 ms tick; the three tab variants reach 5% cumulative energy about 5–19 ms after onset. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-transient-edit.json\">UI edit evidence<\/a><\/p><p>Music lengths are 147.5 seconds for title and boss, and 177.5 seconds for sanctuary and rift. The loop splice spans 2.5 seconds; context changes use a 1.5-second fade. Unselected music pauses. The existing 16 SFX voices, priorities, concurrency controls and final-mix limiter remain. Audio does not mutate saves or combat random streams.<\/p><h2 id=\"maintenance-and-validation\">Maintenance and validation<\/h2><pre><code>python3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/audio_audition.py<\/code><\/pre><p>The full provenance check requires all 458 assets; a partial-completion option is no longer necessary. Retired or unreferenced runtime WAVs and modified originals or masters fail validation. <code>--rebuild<\/code> uses retained sources and skips shared actions, so it creates no duplicate audio. These tools make no API calls and spend no credits.<\/p><h2 id=\"evidence\">Evidence<\/h2><p>Current cleanup validation is recorded in the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json\">cleanup report<\/a> and <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-final-summary.json\">Unity result<\/a>. Checks compare all 458 master hashes and metadata with the baseline, retain every playback identifier, and verify that shared actions play the same imported assets.<\/p><p>31 Unity Edit Mode tests, seven offline tool tests and nine shared UI contract tests passed. The <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-source-validation.json\">full provenance check<\/a> passed for all 458 files with none missing. The macOS development build succeeded with zero errors. Native focused checks passed for all nine shared effects using existing imported assets and listener output, four music transitions/loops, short developer-training runs for three classes, volume/mute and preferences restored after process restart. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-shared-effects.txt\">Shared effects<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-music.txt\">Music<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-audio.txt\">Controls/classes<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-restart.txt\">Restart<\/a><\/p><p>The full gameplay smoke recorded 1,074 events across 76 cues with no missing clips or logged errors. However, after an optional inventory interaction failed, the ranger timed out approaching the rift keeper: <strong>the full smoke failed<\/strong>. Forge interaction was also skipped because its pointer target was blocked. Focused audio success is not substituted for full gameplay success. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-summary.txt\">Full summary<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-trace.tsv\">Trace<\/a><\/p><p>Earlier signal measurements remain applicable to byte-identical masters: all 454 SFX passed with zero clipped samples, maximum absolute DC 0.000260 and approximately -2 dBTP peak. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json\">SFX<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json\">Music<\/a><\/p><p>Earlier music/settings runtime tests covered four streaming tracks, loop progress, transitions, volume, mute and settings restoration after process restart. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt\">Music<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt\">Settings<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt\">Restart<\/a><\/p><p>The macOS gameplay smoke uses synthetic EventSystem input and disposable accounts. Covered town controls may use direct callbacks; optional forge interaction is skipped if pointer access is blocked. This is not physical mobile input or performance evidence. The public wiki is published only from merged <code>main<\/code>.<\/p>", "headings": [{"id": "final-catalog-and-shared-clips", "title": "Final catalog and shared clips"}, {"id": "removal-and-storage", "title": "Removal and storage"}, {"id": "preserved-provenance-and-audio-quality", "title": "Preserved provenance and audio quality"}, {"id": "maintenance-and-validation", "title": "Maintenance and validation"}, {"id": "evidence", "title": "Evidence"}]}, {"body": "# ElevenLabs game audio\n\nWritten: 2026-09-27 · [한국어](ElevenLabs_Game_Audio.md)\n\nThe user accepted the currently adopted audio as the final version. The retained set contains **454 sound effects and four music tracks: 458 files**. It covers all 283 SFX identifiers and four music contexts. Nine SFX actions share suitable existing final clips. No additional generation is planned.\n\nFinal acceptance is based on the user's instruction. It does not claim a new human listening test or physical mobile validation. These changes are on the work branch; merging to `main` and publishing the wiki are separate steps.\n\n## Final catalog and shared clips\n\n274 SFX identifiers have dedicated source generations. The following nine actions reference the same imported `AudioClip` assets as their source cues. They do not copy files or count the same generation as another variation. Action identifiers, cooldowns, priorities and concurrency limits remain intact.\n\n| Action | Final source cue | Reason |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `reward.claim` | `ui.confirm` | Successful reward confirmation |\n| `shop.gamble_beat` | `ui.click_heavy` | Short, weighty reveal beat |\n| `gem.socket` | `item.equip.orb` | A crystal seating in a metal mount |\n| `reward.box_open` | `reward.chest` | A treasure chest with a latch and wooden hinge |\n| `rune.fuse` | `gem.fuse` | Crystal tones converging into one |\n| `rune.place` | `forge.core_invest` | A stone core inserted into a slot |\n| `rune.remove` | `gem.remove` | A release click from a mounted material |\n| `rune.rotate` | `loot.stone` | A short mineral contact |\n| `rune.unlock` | `aspect.upgrade` | A rising arcane-seal resonance |\n\nThe [final catalog](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/sfx-catalog.json) owns mastering targets and shared-cue relationships. It produces the [runtime bank](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Resources/Audio/Sfx/bank.json). The [production list](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json) distinguishes dedicated and shared audio; the previous generation-limit wait is closed.\n\n## Removal and storage\n\n- Removed all 15 remaining procedural WAVs and their `.meta` files after checking for external Unity GUID references. The bytes, GUIDs and import settings of all 458 final assets are preserved.\n- Removed downloaded copies of all 1,087 generation candidates, old preview conversions, duplicated preview masters, previous test builds and temporary test saves. Exactly one retained original per selected generation remains under `AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources`.\n- Removed retired synthesis recipes and synthesis-only code. The historical `generate_sfx.py` command now validates final files, writes bank metadata and produces previews. Running it without an operation fails instead of synthesizing audio.\n- The audition page uses a symbolic link to the actual game masters. Rebuilding it does not duplicate WAV or MP3 files.\n- Git history is unchanged. Removed tracked files can be recovered from pre-cleanup commit `949b31af520249e3c7708c7ef96256099f293cf6`. Other worktrees and the general Unity cache are outside this cleanup.\n\nRetired runtime WAVs occupied 1,504,326 bytes. Final runtime WAVs total 176,891,768 bytes. Task production and validation artifacts decreased from approximately 3.00 GB to 13.7 MB, **saving about 2.98 GB**. The new validation build and temporary accounts were also removed. [Cleanup evidence](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json) records the measurements. Source-storage savings are not measurements of mobile build size or runtime memory savings.\n\n## Preserved provenance and audio quality\n\n| Item | SFX | Music |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MCP-verified model | `eleven_text_to_sound_v2` | `eleven_music_v2` |\n| Generated original | MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps | MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps |\n| Final master | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono | WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo |\n| Unity import | Existing ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory | Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, no preload |\n\nThe [source manifest](../../AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json) records model, generation ID, prompt, parameters and source/master hashes. Originals remain outside Unity builds for reproduction and provenance. Converting an MP3 to WAV does not recover discarded information. Cleanup does not re-encode or reduce the quality of any retained master.\n\nSFX processing uses silence trimming, DC removal, short fades, linear gain and a -2 dBTP ceiling. Slider effects contain one 30 ms tick; the three tab variants reach 5% cumulative energy about 5–19 ms after onset. [UI edit evidence](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-transient-edit.json)\n\nMusic lengths are 147.5 seconds for title and boss, and 177.5 seconds for sanctuary and rift. The loop splice spans 2.5 seconds; context changes use a 1.5-second fade. Unselected music pauses. The existing 16 SFX voices, priorities, concurrency controls and final-mix limiter remain. Audio does not mutate saves or combat random streams.\n\n## Maintenance and validation\n\n```sh\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/audio_audition.py\n```\n\nThe full provenance check requires all 458 assets; a partial-completion option is no longer necessary. Retired or unreferenced runtime WAVs and modified originals or masters fail validation. `--rebuild` uses retained sources and skips shared actions, so it creates no duplicate audio. These tools make no API calls and spend no credits.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent cleanup validation is recorded in the [cleanup report](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json) and [Unity result](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-final-summary.json). Checks compare all 458 master hashes and metadata with the baseline, retain every playback identifier, and verify that shared actions play the same imported assets.\n\n31 Unity Edit Mode tests, seven offline tool tests and nine shared UI contract tests passed. The [full provenance check](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-source-validation.json) passed for all 458 files with none missing. The macOS development build succeeded with zero errors. Native focused checks passed for all nine shared effects using existing imported assets and listener output, four music transitions/loops, short developer-training runs for three classes, volume/mute and preferences restored after process restart. [Shared effects](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-shared-effects.txt) · [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-music.txt) · [Controls/classes](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-audio.txt) · [Restart](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-restart.txt)\n\nThe full gameplay smoke recorded 1,074 events across 76 cues with no missing clips or logged errors. However, after an optional inventory interaction failed, the ranger timed out approaching the rift keeper: **the full smoke failed**. Forge interaction was also skipped because its pointer target was blocked. Focused audio success is not substituted for full gameplay success. [Full summary](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-summary.txt) · [Trace](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-trace.tsv)\n\nEarlier signal measurements remain applicable to byte-identical masters: all 454 SFX passed with zero clipped samples, maximum absolute DC 0.000260 and approximately -2 dBTP peak. [SFX](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json) · [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json)\n\nEarlier music/settings runtime tests covered four streaming tracks, loop progress, transitions, volume, mute and settings restoration after process restart. [Music](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt) · [Settings](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt) · [Restart](ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt)\n\nThe macOS gameplay smoke uses synthetic EventSystem input and disposable accounts. Covered town controls may use direct callbacks; optional forge interaction is skipped if pointer access is blocked. This is not physical mobile input or performance evidence. The public wiki is published only from merged `main`.\n\n## Addition: title login flight sounds (2026-10-14)\n\nTwo new sound effects for the [title login flight](Title_Screen.en.md) were generated with ElevenLabs `eleven_text_to_sound_v2` (MCP, prompt influence 0.65). Four candidates were generated per cue and one was chosen from its loudness envelope.\n\n| Cue | Use | Adopted generation ID | Length |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `flow.title_flight` | Wind rush as the flight starts | `PmH0ZtJAEtC86aHk2V7O` | 1.70 s |\n| `flow.title_rift` | Rift light burst | `e9C3rrKPb3aFTcuHuWXP` | 1.50 s |\n\nThe original MP3s are kept in `AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources/` and were mastered with `elevenlabs_audio.py`. The set is now 456 sound effect files plus four music tracks, with 285 SFX identifiers. The eight generations cost 54.7 credits (the estimate said 180). No human listening check was done.\n\nNote: on the same day `main`'s `sfx-catalog.json` and `bank.json` disagree because of the D4 skill identifier migration, so `generate_sfx.py --check` and `elevenlabs_audio.py --check` fail (they already did before this change). The two new bank rows match the generator's format, and `test_elevenlabs_audio.py` passes.\n", "html": "<p>Written: 2026-09-27 · <a href=\"#/page/elevenlabs-game-audio\">한국어<\/a><\/p><p>The user accepted the currently adopted audio as the final version. The retained set contains <strong>454 sound effects and four music tracks: 458 files<\/strong>. It covers all 283 SFX identifiers and four music contexts. Nine SFX actions share suitable existing final clips. No additional generation is planned.<\/p><p>Final acceptance is based on the user&#x27;s instruction. It does not claim a new human listening test or physical mobile validation. These changes are on the work branch; merging to <code>main<\/code> and publishing the wiki are separate steps.<\/p><h2 id=\"final-catalog-and-shared-clips\">Final catalog and shared clips<\/h2><p>274 SFX identifiers have dedicated source generations. The following nine actions reference the same imported <code>AudioClip<\/code> assets as their source cues. They do not copy files or count the same generation as another variation. Action identifiers, cooldowns, priorities and concurrency limits remain intact.<\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Action<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Final source cue<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Reason<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><code>reward.claim<\/code><\/td><td><code>ui.confirm<\/code><\/td><td>Successful reward confirmation<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>shop.gamble_beat<\/code><\/td><td><code>ui.click_heavy<\/code><\/td><td>Short, weighty reveal beat<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>gem.socket<\/code><\/td><td><code>item.equip.orb<\/code><\/td><td>A crystal seating in a metal mount<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>reward.box_open<\/code><\/td><td><code>reward.chest<\/code><\/td><td>A treasure chest with a latch and wooden hinge<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.fuse<\/code><\/td><td><code>gem.fuse<\/code><\/td><td>Crystal tones converging into one<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.place<\/code><\/td><td><code>forge.core_invest<\/code><\/td><td>A stone core inserted into a slot<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.remove<\/code><\/td><td><code>gem.remove<\/code><\/td><td>A release click from a mounted material<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.rotate<\/code><\/td><td><code>loot.stone<\/code><\/td><td>A short mineral contact<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>rune.unlock<\/code><\/td><td><code>aspect.upgrade<\/code><\/td><td>A rising arcane-seal resonance<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/sfx-catalog.json\">final catalog<\/a> owns mastering targets and shared-cue relationships. It produces the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Resources/Audio/Sfx/bank.json\">runtime bank<\/a>. The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/production-plan.json\">production list<\/a> distinguishes dedicated and shared audio; the previous generation-limit wait is closed.<\/p><h2 id=\"removal-and-storage\">Removal and storage<\/h2><ul><li>Removed all 15 remaining procedural WAVs and their <code>.meta<\/code> files after checking for external Unity GUID references. The bytes, GUIDs and import settings of all 458 final assets are preserved.<\/li><li>Removed downloaded copies of all 1,087 generation candidates, old preview conversions, duplicated preview masters, previous test builds and temporary test saves. Exactly one retained original per selected generation remains under <code>AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources<\/code>.<\/li><li>Removed retired synthesis recipes and synthesis-only code. The historical <code>generate_sfx.py<\/code> command now validates final files, writes bank metadata and produces previews. Running it without an operation fails instead of synthesizing audio.<\/li><li>The audition page uses a symbolic link to the actual game masters. Rebuilding it does not duplicate WAV or MP3 files.<\/li><li>Git history is unchanged. Removed tracked files can be recovered from pre-cleanup commit <code>949b31af520249e3c7708c7ef96256099f293cf6<\/code>. Other worktrees and the general Unity cache are outside this cleanup.<\/li><\/ul><p>Retired runtime WAVs occupied 1,504,326 bytes. Final runtime WAVs total 176,891,768 bytes. Task production and validation artifacts decreased from approximately 3.00 GB to 13.7 MB, <strong>saving about 2.98 GB<\/strong>. The new validation build and temporary accounts were also removed. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json\">Cleanup evidence<\/a> records the measurements. Source-storage savings are not measurements of mobile build size or runtime memory savings.<\/p><h2 id=\"preserved-provenance-and-audio-quality\">Preserved provenance and audio quality<\/h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Item<\/th><th scope=\"col\">SFX<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Music<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>MCP-verified model<\/td><td><code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2<\/code><\/td><td><code>eleven_music_v2<\/code><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Generated original<\/td><td>MP3, 44.1 kHz, stereo, 128 kbps<\/td><td>MP3, 48 kHz, stereo, 192 kbps<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Final master<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, mono<\/td><td>WAV, 48 kHz, PCM16, stereo<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Unity import<\/td><td>Existing ADPCM or Vorbis, compressed in memory<\/td><td>Streaming, Vorbis quality 0.9, stereo, no preload<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The <a href=\"sources/AudioSources/ElevenLabs/manifest.json\">source manifest<\/a> records model, generation ID, prompt, parameters and source/master hashes. Originals remain outside Unity builds for reproduction and provenance. Converting an MP3 to WAV does not recover discarded information. Cleanup does not re-encode or reduce the quality of any retained master.<\/p><p>SFX processing uses silence trimming, DC removal, short fades, linear gain and a -2 dBTP ceiling. Slider effects contain one 30 ms tick; the three tab variants reach 5% cumulative energy about 5–19 ms after onset. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/ui-transient-edit.json\">UI edit evidence<\/a><\/p><p>Music lengths are 147.5 seconds for title and boss, and 177.5 seconds for sanctuary and rift. The loop splice spans 2.5 seconds; context changes use a 1.5-second fade. Unselected music pauses. The existing 16 SFX voices, priorities, concurrency controls and final-mix limiter remain. Audio does not mutate saves or combat random streams.<\/p><h2 id=\"maintenance-and-validation\">Maintenance and validation<\/h2><pre><code>python3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --check\npython3 tools/generate_sfx.py --check --audit Artifacts/audio-bank-audit.json\npython3 tools/test_elevenlabs_audio.py\npython3 tools/elevenlabs_audio.py --rebuild\npython3 tools/audio_audition.py<\/code><\/pre><p>The full provenance check requires all 458 assets; a partial-completion option is no longer necessary. Retired or unreferenced runtime WAVs and modified originals or masters fail validation. <code>--rebuild<\/code> uses retained sources and skips shared actions, so it creates no duplicate audio. These tools make no API calls and spend no credits.<\/p><h2 id=\"evidence\">Evidence<\/h2><p>Current cleanup validation is recorded in the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-cleanup.json\">cleanup report<\/a> and <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/editmode-final-summary.json\">Unity result<\/a>. Checks compare all 458 master hashes and metadata with the baseline, retain every playback identifier, and verify that shared actions play the same imported assets.<\/p><p>31 Unity Edit Mode tests, seven offline tool tests and nine shared UI contract tests passed. The <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/final-source-validation.json\">full provenance check<\/a> passed for all 458 files with none missing. The macOS development build succeeded with zero errors. Native focused checks passed for all nine shared effects using existing imported assets and listener output, four music transitions/loops, short developer-training runs for three classes, volume/mute and preferences restored after process restart. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-shared-effects.txt\">Shared effects<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-music.txt\">Music<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-audio.txt\">Controls/classes<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-final-restart.txt\">Restart<\/a><\/p><p>The full gameplay smoke recorded 1,074 events across 76 cues with no missing clips or logged errors. However, after an optional inventory interaction failed, the ranger timed out approaching the rift keeper: <strong>the full smoke failed<\/strong>. Forge interaction was also skipped because its pointer target was blocked. Focused audio success is not substituted for full gameplay success. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-summary.txt\">Full summary<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-cleanup-full-trace.tsv\">Trace<\/a><\/p><p>Earlier signal measurements remain applicable to byte-identical masters: all 454 SFX passed with zero clipped samples, maximum absolute DC 0.000260 and approximately -2 dBTP peak. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/runtime-master-audit.json\">SFX<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/music-master-audit.json\">Music<\/a><\/p><p>Earlier music/settings runtime tests covered four streaming tracks, loop progress, transitions, volume, mute and settings restoration after process restart. <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-music.txt\">Music<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-initial.txt\">Settings<\/a> · <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/ElevenLabsAudioEvidence/native-audio-restart.txt\">Restart<\/a><\/p><p>The macOS gameplay smoke uses synthetic EventSystem input and disposable accounts. Covered town controls may use direct callbacks; optional forge interaction is skipped if pointer access is blocked. This is not physical mobile input or performance evidence. The public wiki is published only from merged <code>main<\/code>.<\/p><h2 id=\"addition-title-login-flight-sounds-2026-10-14\">Addition: title login flight sounds (2026-10-14)<\/h2><p>Two new sound effects for the <a href=\"#/page/title-screen.en\">title login flight<\/a> were generated with ElevenLabs <code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2<\/code> (MCP, prompt influence 0.65). Four candidates were generated per cue and one was chosen from its loudness envelope.<\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cue<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Use<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Adopted generation ID<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Length<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><code>flow.title_flight<\/code><\/td><td>Wind rush as the flight starts<\/td><td><code>PmH0ZtJAEtC86aHk2V7O<\/code><\/td><td>1.70 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><code>flow.title_rift<\/code><\/td><td>Rift light burst<\/td><td><code>e9C3rrKPb3aFTcuHuWXP<\/code><\/td><td>1.50 s<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The original MP3s are kept in <code>AudioSources/ElevenLabs/Sources/<\/code> and were mastered with <code>elevenlabs_audio.py<\/code>. The set is now 456 sound effect files plus four music tracks, with 285 SFX identifiers. The eight generations cost 54.7 credits (the estimate said 180). No human listening check was done.<\/p><p>Note: on the same day <code>main<\/code>&#x27;s <code>sfx-catalog.json<\/code> and <code>bank.json<\/code> disagree because of the D4 skill identifier migration, so <code>generate_sfx.py --check<\/code> and <code>elevenlabs_audio.py --check<\/code> fail (they already did before this change). The two new bank rows match the generator&#x27;s format, and <code>test_elevenlabs_audio.py<\/code> passes.<\/p>", "headings": [{"id": "final-catalog-and-shared-clips", "title": "Final catalog and shared clips"}, {"id": "removal-and-storage", "title": "Removal and storage"}, {"id": "preserved-provenance-and-audio-quality", "title": "Preserved provenance and audio quality"}, {"id": "maintenance-and-validation", "title": "Maintenance and validation"}, {"id": "evidence", "title": "Evidence"}, {"id": "addition-title-login-flight-sounds-2026-10-14", "title": "Addition: title login flight sounds (2026-10-14)"}]}];
